Description:
The author, rswarbrick, created this PR while tidying up related work in PR #727. The changes were deemed "safe to apply separately" despite uncertainty about the correctness of some modifications in the parent PR.

Commits (5 total):
1. Create fuse_ctrl_mmap.c - Prevents fuse_ctrl_mmap.h from defining instantiated objects that would cause linker failures when included in multiple compilation units.
2. Add documentation for address range type - No functional changes; improves clarity of address range logic in the package.
3. Tidy up tests for Caliptra secret addresses - Updates outdated values in caliptra_ss_fuse_ctrl_manuf_prod_prov from a prior change (275521b1) and applies consistent magic number sourcing to related tests.
4. Avoid hard-coding read lock partitions - Removes hard-coded partition values by generating a template-based map that pulls actual addresses from soc_mmap.h at compile time.
5. Automated pipeline stamp - Microsoft's automated pipeline updated timestamp and hash after successful test run.

